<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Ratlam State</h1><p class="st-meta">1652 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Ratlam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Rathore Rajput state of Malwa founded under Shah Jahan, later known for its trade in opium and gold.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ratlam was granted in 1652 by the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratan-singh-of-ratlam">Ratan Singh</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udai-singh-of-marwar">Raja Udai Singh of Marwar</a>, in reward for service. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sailana-state">Sailana</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sitamau-state">Sitamau</a> later branched off from the same family.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> ruled a fertile plateau of wheat and opium. Ratlam became a trading town known for its markets, gold and the savoury sev that still carries its name. Under British paramountcy it was a salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa-agency">Malwa Agency</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajjan-singh-of-ratlam">Sajjan Singh</a> reigned from 1893 to 1947.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ratlam joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. It is now a district headquarters and a railway junction.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ratlam-state.jpg" alt="Ratlam State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Princely_State_of_Ratlam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1652 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ratlam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ratan Singh, Sajjan Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ratlam</dd></dl></aside></div>
